Well,  if you get into melee combat with a mumak, you're probably going
to lose.

So the answer, then, is, "don't get into melee combat with a mumak".

How to do this? Well, your first big advantage is that you are faster
than it.  Even a normal character can outrun a Mumak.   Once at range,
you have a variety of missile weapons just lying around the dungeon to
use on it ... attack wands, bow and arrows, sling and rocks, crossbow
and bolts, daggers,  and even just throwing rocks.

Heck, if you're being killed by Mumaks you're most likely in the
Gnomish mines.  You could, er, "borrow" a pick-axe from a dwarf and
convert any boulder into 30-40+ rocks.  You've got as many missile
weapons as you want, they never go away, and I don't believe they're
ever cursed.

The other problem is that you might bump into a Mumak in the dark.
The solution, then, is vision that stretches further than one space in
every direction.   The most obvious solution is a light such as a
candle or a lamp -- and Itzhak's Light Shop isn't a guaranteed shop in
Minetown for no reason :).    Or you could start as an elf, dwarf, or
orc which have infravision and can see things like Mumaks a long way
away even without a light source.  There are other, more esoteric
methods, but those are spoilers.

If I am forced into melee with a mumak I will write "Elbereth" in the
dust on the ground beneath me and hold *absolutely still* by pressing
the "." key until it loses interest and backs off a space. Then I run
like hell.

Good luck, and see you at the Demigod Bar.

